# Design and UI

## Stack

- **Tailwind CSS v4** with `@import "tailwindcss"`; prefer utility classes and `@theme` tokens over one-off magic values.
- **Next.js App Router** (`app/`); client components only when interactivity or browser APIs require it.

## Color and typography

- Use **semantic CSS variables** from `app/globals.css` (`:root` and `@theme inline`): primary palette (`--color-primary`, `--color-primary-dark`, `--color-primary-mid`, `--color-surface`, `--color-accent-yellow`, `--color-error`), plus `--background`, `--foreground`, `--card`, `--border`.
- Prefer `var(--…)` / theme-mapped Tailwind colors over hard-coded hex in new code unless adding a new token in `globals.css`.
- Body and UI use **Plus Jakarta Sans** (`--font-sans`); **Newsreader** via `.font-display` for logo, hero, and major headings only; monospace uses **Space Mono** (`--font-mono`).

## Layout and polish

- Avoid horizontal overflow on small viewports (`overflow-x: hidden` is set on `html, body`); do not reintroduce full-width overflow with fixed-width children.
- Keep **spacing, type scale, and borders** consistent with existing components (`components/`, `app/`).
- Respect existing patterns such as **flip-card** auth UI (`.flip-card-*` classes) when touching those surfaces.

## Accessibility

- Interactive elements need visible **focus** states and sufficient **contrast** against `--background` / `--card`.
- Use semantic HTML (headings, landmarks, labels for form controls).
